# Line endings, the same on every machine. Git stores text with LF, and without these rules a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF. Terraform then reads a different string in
# every heredoc than the one it applied and plans to replace the resource
*.tf     text eol=lf
*.tftpl  text eol=lf
*.hcl    text eol=lf
# Startup scripts run on Linux, where a CR at the end of the shebang line breaks the interpreter
*.sh     text eol=lf
# The k3s config files and manifests become the node's user data. A CRLF checkout would change
# that text, and with it the instance, which is replaced on any user data change
*.yaml   text eol=lf
